# Shapeover

Shapeover is a lightweight Chrome and Edge extension for covering parts of a website with custom shapes or image fills. Covers are saved for the current site origin and positioned in document coordinates, so they stay attached to the page while you scroll.

## Install in Chrome or Edge

1. Open `chrome://extensions` in Chrome or `edge://extensions` in Edge.
2. Turn on **Developer mode**.
3. Choose **Load unpacked** and select this project folder.
4. Open or refresh a regular website, then select the Shapeover toolbar button.

## Draw a cover

Choose freehand, rectangle, oval, or polygon.

Select **On page** to keep a cover attached to page coordinates as you scroll, or **Stick** to keep it in the same screen position; sticky covers preserve their distance from the right edge when the window is resized.

New covers default to On page.

Drag to draw the first three shapes. For a polygon, click to place points and press Enter (or double click) to finish.

Choose a solid color or upload an image, and adjust opacity before drawing.

Undo removes the last cover; Clear removes the covers saved for the current site.

Select Done or press Escape to leave the editor.

On page covers use document coordinates and redraw as the page scrolls. Sticky covers stay in the viewport and preserve their distance from its right edge.

Covers and image fills are stored locally in the browser under the current page origin.

## Files

- `manifest.json` — Manifest V3 extension config
- `popup.html`, `popup.css`, `popup.js` — toolbar popup
- `content.js` — on-page editor, drawing and local persistence

